# armour/shared/pauldron_layered3_l: the medium LAYERED pauldron on the left shoulder (layered.3; FORGE-SHOULDERS, STYLE_P2 28.3).
# lamellar flaps laced in steps: each row of lamellae a step lower and a pixel further out, its lacing a row of
# dots (Jade, Steppe, Dune, Marsh, Sylvan).
# Rides the lean and the bob and lifts a pixel on wind-ups (`up`). Finish regions: R the lowest flap's hem, G the top lacing knot, N the lacing rows, P the flaps.
# Shared by the man and the woman (D10). Generated by FORGE-SHOULDERS gen.py from shapes.py (re-run, never hand-edit
# the derived views). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# The rest views repeat as `when shoulder-layered` overlays: the shape's own drawing, which the body's cut skips.
use person
role pauldron layered.3
layer armNear
anchor shoulderL
keys pauld
z 5
side L

